    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0480" n="1214" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1214"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Taylor.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-05"><hi rendition="#italic">July 5,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 363.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit for your information and files a
                    copy of a dispatch from the vice-consul-general of the United States at Havana,
                    No. 2517, of the 19th ultimo, concerning the inquiry of three Cuban landowners,
                    American citizens, residents of Sancti Spiritus, respecting the protection of
                    their property from seizure or destruction by insurgents. I add also a copy of
                    the Department’s reply, No. 1098, of the 1st instant, indicating the general
                    principles applicable in such cases.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>






